{"nodes": [{"id": "_planning_phases_04_durable_generation_and_accepted_quality_04_ai_spec_document", "label": "04-AI-SPEC.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".planning/phases/04-durable-generation-and-accepted-quality/04-AI-SPEC.md", "source_location": "$graphify-root$/.planning/phases/04-durable-generation-and-accepted-quality/04-AI-SPEC.md:1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "document_context": "Historical planning or evidence; claims are source assertions, not independently verified current runtime facts.", "rationale": [{"text": "**Stakes Level:** High. A polished but inaccurate campaign can mislead customers, damage a local business's reputation and send orders or bookings to the wrong offer. The stakes are critical for clinic/pharmacy-adjacent content because misleading health claims, unapproved price promotions, or patient exposure create regulatory and patient-privacy harm.", "source_location": "$graphify-root$/.planning/phases/04-durable-generation-and-accepted-quality/04-AI-SPEC.md:30"}, {"text": "| Framework | Ruled Out Because |", "source_location": "$graphify-root$/.planning/phases/04-durable-generation-and-accepted-quality/04-AI-SPEC.md:112"}, {"text": "2. **Submitting after a timeout or invalid start response.** Remote acceptance may already have succeeded. Reconcile the same idempotency key/opaque operation; never create a second customer attempt merely because the start response was lost.", "source_location": "$graphify-root$/.planning/phases/04-durable-generation-and-accepted-quality/04-AI-SPEC.md:208"}, {"text": "The canonical production contract is Zod because the worker is TypeScript. Every AI quality response must parse exactly, contain all required dimensions, and be sent through the deterministic `evaluateAcceptedOutput` policy. Do not parse model prose or coerce absent values.", "source_location": "$graphify-root$/.planning/phases/04-durable-generation-and-accepted-quality/04-AI-SPEC.md